<title>USA: Chase Brass Q4 shr $0.53 vs $0.41.</title>
<headline>Chase Brass Q4 shr $0.53 vs $0.41.</headline>
<dateline>MONTPELIER, Ohio 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>CHASE BRASS INDUSTRIES, INC.</p>
<p>		 (In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>	  Quarter Ended December 31,    Year Ended December 31,</p>
<p>		    1996     1995  % Chg	1996    1995  % Chg</p>
<p> Net sales     $106,726 $75,294    42   $366,991 $313,097  17</p>
<p>Operating income</p>
<p>		     10,263   7,070    45     36,815  29,274   26</p>
<p>   Net income     5,325   4,109    29     20,639  16,701   23</p>
<p>Average shares</p>
<p>   outstanding   10,065  10,061    --     10,063  10,061   --</p>
<p>Earnings per share</p>
<p>			 0.53    0.41    29	 2.05    1.66   23</p>
<p>NOTE: Since being acquired August 30, 1996, from UNR Industries Inc, Leavitt Tube added $49.3 million to net sales and contributed six cents per share to earnings after interest expense associated with the acquisition debt. In addition, the earnings per share contribution is after deducting about three cents per share as a result of converting the Leavitt operations from the first-in, first-out basis of accounting for inventories to the last-in, first-out basis.</p>
